//     invariant is preserved after Phase 0.
//
//   Phase 1 (unconstrained loop): We only enter this loop when
//     `!insideConstrainedOut`, and the loop body never sets insideConstrainedOut
//     to true (we intentionally skip entering constrained mode). Therefore the
//     antecedent of the invariant is false throughout the loop body, and the
//     invariant holds trivially in every iteration.
//
//   Phase 2 (OpenConstrainedSpan): sets insideConstrainedOut := true and
//     currentConstrainedOut := []. The precondition `parser.IsValidPrefix([])`
//     is stated in the method's requires clause, so the invariant holds.
//
//   Phase 3 (CloseSpanWithinBudget): The postcondition guarantees
//     `insideOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentOut)`, preserving the invariant.
//
// Invariant 2: progress
//   |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
//
//   Initialization: generated := generatedPrefix and steps := 0, so equality holds.
//
//   Phase 0: CloseSpanWithinBudget appends at most `ib` tokens to `generated`
//     and steps is incremented by exactly `ib`, preserving the bound.
//
//   Phase 1 loop: Each iteration increments `steps` by 1. If EOS is sampled,
//     we break without appending to generated, so |generated| is unchanged while
//     steps grows by 1; the bound is still satisfied. If a non-EOS token is
//     sampled, |generated| grows by exactly 1 = delta steps. In both cases
//     |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps is preserved.
//
//   Phase 2: OpenConstrainedSpan appends exactly 1 delimiter token, so
//     |generated| grows by 1 and steps grows by 1 simultaneously.
//
